        <p>Non-exempt hourly workers earn at least time and a half past 40 hours in a workweek under the Fair Labor Standards Act. At $52.00 an hour, that’s $78.00 an overtime hour. Five extra hours a week, every week, is the most common pattern, and it is worth pricing properly:</p>
